name=Cookie Slicer
id=CookieSlicer
description=Cookie Cheetah's own performance mod (AKA). The Cookie Slicer button on the main menu (top right) and the F8 key in game (Options > Mods to change) open a big black / mint window (Thai / English) with three pages. Performance: your PC now (FPS, game RAM, PC RAM, CPU, game main thread; point at a number to see what it means and how yours looks), what the chosen settings should save (about), FPS measured before / after a change, and the settings: levels Undo all / Balanced / Smooth / Max plus one switch per setting (the game's own options that cost CPU / RAM for little you can see: unseen zombies update less, plain zombie clothes, no blood on weapons, windows drawn 30 times a second, lighting 15 per second, at most 10 ragdolls; weak PC after a restart: compressed textures, textures up to 1024, no corpse shadows). Shader: with the Cookie Slicer Helper v1.1.0, a real screen shader drawn after the game's own one (media/shaders/cookie_post.*): 8 styles (Natural, Golden Hour, True Film, Night Glow, Vivid, Cinema, Retro, Intense Dark) with sliders (strength, brightness, contrast, colour, warm / cool, glow, dark edges, sharpness, grain), a check whether this PC can run it (helper, graphics card, OpenGL, measured ms per frame), quality Auto / Low / Medium / High, "Fit my PC", and a before / after line on the live game; about 11 MB of graphics memory at 1080p, no PC RAM. Without the helper: basic looks (Natural, Cinema, Retro, Intense Dark) and brightness, no FPS cost. Version Slicer: mod and helper versions, game RAM, how to install / update / remove the helper; with the helper v1.2.0 also Java's RAM savers (on / off, from the next start), RAM held / really used, and "What uses the RAM" (the biggest parts of the game's memory, saved as Zomboid/Lua/CookieSlicer_heap.txt). In game the window is see-through (switch in its header); on the main menu it hides while the server list or another menu screen is open. Before you join: a small panel next to the server list and the connecting screen shows the helper, game RAM, free PC RAM, ProjectZomboid64.json (PZ Optimization left in it) and why the last join failed with the steps to fix it (the game's message; with the helper also what it found in the game's log, Zomboid/Lua/CookieSlicer_diag.txt). Map loading: the work every mod does for each map square that loads runs a little at a time over the next frames, and work only the server needs is skipped in players' games (Cookie Square Queue). Cookie Profiler measures each mod's Lua time when Zomboid/Lua/CookieProfile_client.txt or CookieProfile_server.txt exists. Optional Cookie Slicer Helper (installed outside the game) adds CPU / RAM numbers and more RAM for the game. Keep it at the top of the mod list.
